  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186059848,
      "id": "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93",
      "title": "Identifying Singular Matrices"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4babbbbb-b2ef-50a6-b25c-023b37598137",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $R$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(R)=0$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2 \\sqrt{2} & - \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ - 5 \\sqrt{2} & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2 \\sqrt{2} & - \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ - 5 \\sqrt{2} & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2})|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{3}{2})|\\begin{aligned}2 \\sqrt{2} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ - 5 \\sqrt{2} & \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}2 \\sqrt{2} & - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ - 5 \\sqrt{2} & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2})(- 2 \\sqrt{2}- 3 \\sqrt{2})+(- \\frac{3}{2})(\\frac{16}{3}+\\frac{20}{3})+\\sqrt{2}(9 \\sqrt{2}- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot (- 5 \\sqrt{2})+(- \\frac{3}{2})\\cdot 12+\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =15-18+3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "896cc58c-6d9c-5986-b32f-f3629548fb9b",
